# Async SNN Inference — N-MNIST (`sepi_tmlr_jax_syncL1_1006_v2.py`)

Frame-based asynchronous SNN inference on N-MNIST using JAX and MPI.

## MPI Pipeline

```
rank 0        —  input feeder
rank 1        —  sync LIF  (fires once per frame at frame-end)
rank 2 … N-2  —  async LIF (fires every forward_group_size events)
rank N-1      —  output accumulator
```

Number of ranks = number of layers (e.g. `[2312, 64, 64, 64, 10]` → `mpirun -n 5`).

## Run

```bash
# Basic inference
mpirun -n 5 python sepi_tmlr_jax_syncL1_1006_v2.py --config sepi_tmlr_conf_5layer.yaml

# Quick test (50 samples)
mpirun -n 5 python sepi_tmlr_jax_syncL1_1006_v2.py --config sepi_tmlr_conf_5layer.yaml --max_samples 50

# Save per-sample stats to Excel + CSV
mpirun -n 5 python sepi_tmlr_jax_syncL1_1006_v2.py --config sepi_tmlr_conf_5layer.yaml --out_stats results
```

## Key Config Fields (YAML)

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `layer_sizes` | Network architecture |
| `weight_file` | Path to `.npz` weights (`arr_0`, `arr_1`, …) |
| `forward_group_size` | Async fire rate (events before firing) |
| `threshold` | Firing threshold |
| `tau_m` | Membrane time constant (ms) |
| `time_window` | Frame duration (ms) |
| `use_refrac` | Refractory within frames |

## CLI Arguments

| Argument | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `--config` | YAML config path |
| `--max_samples` | Limit test samples |
| `--fgs` | Override `forward_group_size` |
| `--scheduler` | `momentum` (default) or `random` |
| `--out_stats` | Save per-sample stats to `.xlsx` and `.csv` |
| `--benchmark` | Sweep fgs × scheduler × use_refrac |

## Output (`--out_stats`)

Saves one row per sample: `sample, label, pred, correct, input_ev, hid_spk, L1_ev … LN_ev, t_ms`

